</p/><p><strong>Summary: </strong>
Exploring my personal multitudes.
</p>
        <p>I’m in a bit of a blogging desert.  In part because my daily life feels full and
rich.  I’ve been learning about my attachment styles and working hard on
becoming a better person.</p>
<p>This has meant lots of crying; of digging through my multitudes; of talking and
listening; of being vulnerable and trusting.</p>
<p>Growing pains, once I felt in youth the ache in my knees.  Now, I feel it in my
soul.  A discomfort that I know is my traversing a path towards a greater self.</p>
<p>Recently, I was sharing with my partner that I feel as though I am both the oak
and the acorn.  And at present, resonating most with the acorn.  I carry the
memories of that oak tree, but am experiencing a spiritual rebirth and
awakening.</p>
<p>Yet I am still that oak tree, slowly healing the damages of wind storms that
once rended my limbs.  I carry those scars and that seedling-that-is-me sees
that old-oak-that-is-me, acknowledging the scars yet feeling a tender
suppleness as those stormy winds mean something different.</p>
<blockquote class="verse" data-id="haiku-attr-shortcode-date-2026-05-16">
Confident oak leaf<br />
Unfurl and breath deep this day<br />
Sapling see your sire<br />
</blockquote>

